    "description": {
      "summary": "The Mothman is a cryptid that reportedly appeared in Point Pleasant, West Virginia and surrounding areas between November 1966 and December 1967.",
      "full": "The Mothman is a cryptid that reportedly appeared in Point Pleasant, West Virginia and surrounding areas between November 1966 and December 1967. Witnesses described a large, man-sized or larger creature with enormous wings and glowing red eyes. The Mothman phenomenon became inextricably linked to the collapse of the Silver Bridge on December 15, 1967, which killed 46 people. This association has led to Mothman's reputation as an omen or harbinger of disaster. The town of Point Pleasant has embraced the legend with a museum, 12-foot statue, and annual festival."
    },
